// Pull request author: Kvvvvvvvvv
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Driver or Device Removal via PnPUtil
// Sigma ID: decca722-d099-46df-b6c0-288634960122
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Keerthivasan
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects when a driver is deleted/uninstalled or a device is disabled/removed using the built-in
//   Plug and Play Utility (pnputil.exe). This behavior is often observed when threat actors attempt
//   to disable security product drivers (defense evasion) or uninstall drivers after exploiting them
//   (BYOVD clean-up).
// False positives:
//   - System administrators or deployment scripts updating drivers by removing old versions.
//   - Antivirus or hardware OEM software updates (e.g. Dell, Lenovo, HP update managers).
//   - VMware Tools, VirtualBox Guest Additions, or other VM guest integration agent updates.
//   - Device drivers uninstallation during legitimate system maintenance.
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/devtest/pnputil-command-syntax
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/threat-hunting-driver-tampering/
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2022/12/12/investigating-impairment-of-defenses/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/72637528be8f6a15c3192dda7d0dfcc49472d7bd/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pnputil_driver_device_removal.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\pnputil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "pnputil.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "delete-driver" or ProcessCommandLine contains "disable-device" or ProcessCommandLine contains "remove-device")
